  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Do The ?** (1 review): Listener believes the sixth track is titled \"Do The Two\" (or \"Do The 2\") [4]\n- **Move On Up** (1 other source): Move On Up is marked as segueing straight into Keep On Pushin [2]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Do The ?**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Baby I Do Love Ya**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Flurries**: back after 22 archived shows (497 days) [5]\n- **Signed, Sealed, Delivered, I'm Yours**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [5]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n- **Keep On Pushin'**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [5]\n- **Joy & Pain**: rare: 4 archived performances [5]\n- **Move On Up**: rare: 11 archived performances [5]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2010-09-11.sunboy.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 133 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]\n- **soulive2010-09-11.akg.flac16**: source not stated; 12 songs; 133 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2010-09-11.sunboy.flac16**: taped by Steven Weld; transferred by Steven Weld; source: 2 Neumann SKM 140’s(AK40 caps/LC3 actives/KM100)>>GAKables xlr>Lunatec V2>GAKables xlr>Apogee Mini-Me@96/24>AES/EBU>Sound Devices 722 @96kHz/24bit [1]. Also: Recorded with two Neumann SKM 140 mics with AK40 capsules, DIN pattern at 90 degrees, on a stand at nine feet, about 25 feet from the stage; Master was moved by firewire into Sound Forge, resampled to 44.1kHz/16-bit, tracked, tagged and encoded to FLAC level 8 [1]\n- **soulive2010-09-11.akg.flac16**: taped by W Clark; transferred by W Clark; source: AKG 483 > LB > M10 [2]",
